{"ok":true,"data":{"papers":[{"id":"857ec5a0-62c9-42ae-80f7-498f354610f6","project_id":"eb3647ac-5ff6-421d-b26d-ab066b058d42","doi":"10.1126/science.aan5348","pmid":"28818941","title":"A molecular spin-photovoltaic device","authors":[{"author_id":"https://openalex.org/A5038958392","name":"Xiangnan Sun","affiliation":"National Center for Nanoscience and Technology","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5461-9699","is_corresponding":false,"h_index":45.0},{"author_id":"https://openalex.org/A5004133391","name":"Saül Vélez","affiliation":"CIC nanoGUNE","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0019-2271","is_corresponding":false,"h_index":30.0},{"author_id":"https://openalex.org/A5064274955","name":"Ainhoa Atxabal","affiliation":"CIC nanoGUNE","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2661-6252","is_corresponding":false,"h_index":15.0},{"author_id":"https://openalex.org/A5075168222","name":"Amilcar Bedoya‐Pinto","affiliation":"Max Planck Institute of Microstructure Physics","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5449-3179","is_corresponding":false,"h_index":26.0},{"author_id":"https://openalex.org/A5008067652","name":"Subir Parui","affiliation":"CIC nanoGUNE","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9722-2552","is_corresponding":false,"h_index":13.0},{"author_id":"https://openalex.org/A5103997497","name":"Xiangwei Zhu","affiliation":"National Center for Nanoscience and Technology","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0009-0003-0232-923X","is_corresponding":false,"h_index":23.0},{"author_id":"https://openalex.org/A5030963266","name":"Roger Llopis","affiliation":"CIC nanoGUNE","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5172-2690","is_corresponding":false,"h_index":18.0},{"author_id":"https://openalex.org/A5084251052","name":"Fèlix Casanova","affiliation":"Ikerbasque","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0316-2163","is_corresponding":false,"h_index":57.0},{"author_id":"https://openalex.org/A5067001459","name":"Luis E. Hueso","affiliation":"Ikerbasque","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7918-8047","is_corresponding":true,"h_index":62.0}],"journal":"Science","publication_year":2017,"cited_by_count":195,"citation_percentile":100.0,"impact_factor":null,"jcr_quartile":null,"cas_zone":null,"journal_percentile":95.5,"field_of_study":"Electrical and Electronic Engineering","abstract":"fullerene-based molecular spin-photovoltaic device that integrates a photovoltaic response with the spin transport across the molecular layer. The photovoltaic response can be modified under the application of a small magnetic field, with a magnetophotovoltage of up to 5% at room temperature. Device functionalities include a magnetic current inverter and the presence of diverging magnetocurrent at certain illumination levels that could be useful for sensing. Completely spin-polarized currents can be created by balancing the external partially spin-polarized injection with the photogenerated carriers.","keywords":["Photovoltaic system","Spin (aerodynamics)","Materials science","Engineering physics","Physics","Engineering","Electrical engineering"],"status":"metadata_ok","has_fulltext":false,"missing_fields":[],"is_classic":false,"is_retracted":false,"created_at":"2026-08-16T07:46:33.189555","updated_at":"2026-08-16T07:46:36.932108","evaluation":null}],"skipped":[],"errors":[]},"warnings":[]}